# The baseline renders themselves are not committed: 70 PNGs at 2x plus the takes they were
# rendered from come to a third of a gigabyte, and dine_ui_snapshots is not deterministic
# (the same build renders most screens a pixel or two apart), so a committed PNG could not be
# diffed anyway. What is committed is the record beside them - the frame costs, the benchmark,
# the RTSan run and the stems the renders were made from - and the commands in README.md,
# which put the images back.
*.png
take/
shots/
sizes/
